    "4": {
      "note": "A record-only repair is checked on the last recorded round only when every candidate finding is closed and candidate bytes are identical; begin_review is not called and the count stays. A repair that changes the candidate uses the ordinary next round; a clean sync with passing focused tests sends no new freeze and begins no round. Fix verification within the settings limit is an ordinary round; a beyond-limit round needs recorded architect/developer approval, not the superseded unconditional D107 further-look account. Separate MEMORY reports/counts do not reset CODE.",
